# --- TIER 1 PLACEHOLDER COLLAPSE (PRIME 2026-08-06) ---
# Three rules replacing 112 static ones, using TWO placeholders each: the
# locale and the trailing slug. Cloudflare documents both (:name matches all
# characters except the path delimiter, and each name may appear once in the
# source and once in the destination).
#
# *** THIS IS A DELIBERATE PROBE, NOT THE FULL COLLAPSE. ***
# A full locale-collapse would take the file from 1,163 rules to 245 - a 79%
# reduction - but it would consume all 100 dynamic slots and stake ~1,000 live
# URLs on a mechanism verified only from documentation. A 2023 wrangler bug
# (workers-sdk#2671) had placeholders resolving to the literal token on direct
# upload; that was Pages, and this deploys to Workers, but it has not been
# proven on THIS path.
#
# These three cover dev-fun, about/history and dev/other - low-traffic paths
# where a failure costs little.
#
# *** CORRECTED 2026-08-30. *** The dev/other rule was written with a :slug
# placeholder, which was wrong: dev-fun and about/history were whole-directory
# moves, where generalising the slug is correct, but dev/other was a move of
# ONE tool (rdap-lookup) out of a room that kept living. The placeholder
# captured every path in the room, so all five green-room tools answered 301
# into /dev/out/<slug>/, where nothing of that name exists - a 404 per tool,
# per locale, for three weeks. Collapse the LOCALE freely; collapse the SLUG
# only when the entire directory moved. check-redirect-shadowing.mjs now
# fails the build if any rule stands in front of a page that exists. If they resolve correctly in production, the
# mechanism is proven and the remaining 890 rules can follow safely.

/:locale/dev-fun/:slug/  /:locale/dev/fun/:slug/  301
/:locale/about/history/:slug/  /:locale/about/:slug/  301
/:locale/dev/other/rdap-lookup/  /:locale/dev/out/rdap-lookup/  301

# Same three collapses for the NO-TRAILING-SLASH variants. Every path in this
# file exists twice - with and without the slash - so a placeholder rule that
# ends in / only covers half of them. Caught by the render probe, which found
# the unslashed statics still present after the first pass.

/:locale/dev-fun/:slug  /:locale/dev/fun/:slug/  301
/:locale/about/history/:slug  /:locale/about/:slug/  301
/:locale/dev/other/rdap-lookup  /:locale/dev/out/rdap-lookup/  301

